W10 the image: ascending 32-bit LE stores of the FW entry of the 0128 container from the RAM base (bytes beyond the length stored as 0), checked per 64 KiB chunk against the CRC of the source bytes and
at the end against the container's CRC32 over the whole read-back (no constant of it in code). The CA7 stays halted; nothing is released.
Pure part (bsd/dev/sweet_wlan_wr.h, tuples SWT_WIN2_TAIL, SWT_LAST_LO, SWT_LAST_HI, SWT_WIN2_ZERO, SWT_IMG, run 2; range field .hi; flags SWT_BULK/SWT_TAIL/SWT_LAST; steps swl_w8..swl_w10):
every store still goes through the one swl_wr(); a BULK word re-reads the preconditions, the live BAR2 window and the old word only at the first word of each 64 KiB chunk and has no per-word read-back (the chunk CRC is the read-back).
Glue (bsd/dev/sweet_wlan.c): sw_fw_note() keeps the FW entry swf_parse() accepted, sweet_wlan_stage3() hands it over, sw3_wr() allows cfg 0x84 only as 0/0x400000 and BAR2 only in the table's two windows and bound to the live cfg 0x84.
